# AI-slop blocklist (SL)

This is the short form. Before writing code in this area, read the full rules with reasons, bad/good examples and checks: `.ui-polish/rules/05-ai-slop.md`.

- **SL-01 No purple/indigo-to-blue gradients** (error). Do not use violet, purple or indigo gradients running to blue, cyan or pink (`from-purple-500 to-blue-500`, `#6366f1 → #8b5cf6`), as backgrounds, buttons, borders or blobs. Default to flat surfaces from the tokens. If the brand in `design.md` has a gradient, build it from the brand tokens and use it in one place.
- **SL-02 No gradient text** (warning). Headings and labels are a solid foreground colour. Do not use `bg-clip-text text-transparent` or `background-clip: text`. For emphasis use weight, size, the display typeface, or the primary colour on one or two words.
- **SL-03 No emoji as icons** (warning). Do not put emoji in buttons, headings, navigation, feature lists, badges, toasts or empty states. Use icons from the project's one icon set (lucide-react in the recipes), sized and coloured by tokens. Emoji are acceptable only as user-generated content or where `design.md` makes them part of the brand voice.
- **SL-04 One icon set** (warning). Import icons from exactly one library, at one stroke width, on a fixed size grid (16px in dense UI, 20px default, 24px for standalone). If the set lacks an icon, draw or adapt one in the same style rather than importing a second library. Brand logos come from one logo source.
- **SL-05 Glass is an exception, not a surface style** (warning). Do not apply `backdrop-blur` with translucent backgrounds to cards, panels, modals and inputs as a house style. Use solid token surfaces (`bg-card`, `bg-popover`). Blur is acceptable on at most one layer that genuinely overlaps scrolling content, such as a sticky header, with an opaque fallback.
- **SL-06 No glows or coloured shadows** (warning). Shadows express elevation only: neutral, low opacity, offset downward, from the four shadow tokens. No `0 0 40px` coloured glows, neon outlines, coloured drop shadows under buttons (`shadow-purple-500/50`) or glowing text. Most surfaces need a border or a shadow, not both, and flat is a valid choice.
- **SL-07 No generic hero copy** (warning). Headlines state what the product does, for whom, with a specific outcome. Ban list: "Supercharge your…", "Unlock the power of…", "Revolutionize…", "Elevate your…", "Seamless", "next-level", "cutting-edge", "all-in-one platform", "Build faster, ship faster", "Welcome to our website", "Transform the way you…". If the product is unknown, ask for it or read the README; do not invent a slogan.
- **SL-08 Not three identical feature cards** (warning). Do not default to a row of three equal cards, each with an icon in a tinted square, a two-word title and one sentence. Structure the content by what it is: a comparison becomes a table, a process becomes numbered steps, a main benefit gets a large block with a real screenshot while secondary ones become a compact list. Vary size by importance. The same applies to the page skeleton "hero, three cards, testimonials, pricing, CTA".
- **SL-09 Radius is restrained and consistent** (warning). Use the radius scale from tokens: small (controls inside controls, 4px), medium (inputs, buttons, 6px), large (cards, dialogs, 8px), and full only for pills, avatars and switches. An inner element's radius is smaller than its container's (outer radius minus the padding between them). Do not round everything to `rounded-2xl` / `rounded-3xl`, and do not mix sharp and very round corners on one screen.
- **SL-10 Not everything is centred** (warning). Left-align body text, forms, lists, tables, settings and dashboards (start-align in RTL). Centre only short, self-contained blocks: a hero headline of one or two lines, an empty state, a confirmation dialog. Never centre paragraphs longer than two lines or form fields.
- **SL-11 No stock dashboard filler** (warning). A dashboard shows what this product's user needs to decide or do next. Do not generate the stock set: four KPI cards ("Total Revenue $45,231.89 +20.1%"), a decorative line chart, "Recent Sales" with avatar initials. Derive metrics from the product's domain (ask or read the data model), give each number a unit, a period and a comparison that is true for the sample data, and leave out a chart when a number or a table answers the question better.
- **SL-12 No decorative noise** (info). Remove decoration that carries no content: blurred colour blobs behind the hero, dot or grid backgrounds, floating shapes, sparkle icons, "New" pills above every headline, animated gradient borders, a rotating logo marquee of invented companies, fake testimonials and star ratings. Use real product screenshots, real customer logos or nothing. Whitespace is a finish, not an absence.
